    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46698" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭpĕr-extendo</span></b> ,
			ĕre, 3, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to stretch over</i>,
				<i>cause to cover</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in aliquo cutem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Ezek. 37, 6</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To stretch excessively</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					2 Cor. 10, 14</span></i>
			.</div>
